  "preamble": "The palatalized stop [dʲ] becoming the voiced postalveolar fricative [ʒ]. The clearest case is the Ukrainian reflex of the Proto-Slavic palatalized stop *ď [dʲ]: *meďa 'border' > межа [meˈʒa], *saďa 'soot' > сажа [ˈsaʒɐ], *pręďa 'yarn' > пряжа [ˈprʲaʒɐ]. Other Slavic languages show different reflexes of the same *ď: Polish and Slovak dz, Czech z, Shtokavian đ [dʑ], Slovene j, Old Church Slavonic and Bulgarian žd, and Russian and Belarusian retroflex ж [ʐ].",
  "phoneticEffects": "Spirantization, Assibilation",
